WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.710
Nikolai Bondarenko is on a political diet.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.840
For nearly a whole month now, the parliamentarian
from Saratov has based his food budget on

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:17.150
a local pensioners' living wage, spending
just 3500 Roubles – or around 46 Euros - to

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.150
eat.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.650
The communist party politician only buys the
bare basics - and says he has been hungry

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.650
all month.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:29.080
I decided to use my own example to prove that
living on 3500 roubles a month is impossible

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.090
without a negative effect on your health.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:39.280
Some accuse the politician of populism, others
here at Saratov market thank him: Bondarenko

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.109
is pushing to double the living wage in Russia.

00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:46.979
His campaign has gotten a huge amount of media
attention – along with us, a Russian federal

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:50.360
TV crew is also filming him preparing his
rations.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.469
But to Bondarenko, this is more than just
PR and bigger than his health.

00:00:55.469 --> 00:01:01.350
I'm convinced that a month on this diet isn't
enough to seriously damage a normal person's

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.999
health in the long-term.

00:01:02.999 --> 00:01:05.390
Of course I have worried about my health.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:11.600
But what I see across the country scares me
much more.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.500
Bondarenko has documented the experiment on
his video blog – and also shows the debate

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.430
that kicked it all off.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.860
Saratov's Labour Minister Natalya Sokolova
insisted the living wage is enough to guarantee

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.530
a balanced diet.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:28.350
She was fired over the remarks
And Bondarenko’s argument has grown into

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.700
a national debate - even on state television.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:37.250
But the government, including Saratov's new
interim minister for labor says the living

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.460
wage will stay the same for now.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:46.750
The living wage is a substantiated sum, based
on statistical calculations - and on the law.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:51.920
Of course we are striving to improve our approach
– in order to work out new, more effective

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.000
methods for calculating the living wage.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.280
That work has begun and should be finished
in 2020.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.100
Bondarenko’s experiment has struck a chord
beyond Saratov.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.490
Across Russia, the standard of living has
been dropping consistently.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:09.310
The Russian government has made halving poverty
a goal for the next six years.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.800
Currently every eighth person in the country
lives under the poverty line – which means

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.180
they earn less than the living wage.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:20.560
Food prices are going up, prices for bread
and milk are going up but the existence minimum

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.800
is still tiny.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:27.980
I can hardly survive
You can only buy the cheapest products on

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.530
3500 thousand.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.450
You can only exist on them, you can’t live.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:37.030
At his office at the Duma, Nikolai Bondarenko's
phone has hardly stopped ringing.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:41.140
The communist politician is convinced that
his words about the living wage will be heard

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.340
on a national level.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:47.430
The only thing the government can’t control
is our solidarity on issues we can unite all

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.430
on.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.209
The government is concerned about this – and
they'd rather lose a finger than a whole hand

00:02:52.209 --> 00:02:56.590
Bondarenko is now preparing to take a draft
bill to the Russian Duma – he wants his

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:03.910
voice to be heard beyond the hallways of the
local parliament.

